orthant 1 language

- # `↯/s.97.1` — `Semver.Error`
+ # `↯/s.97.1` — `Semver.Error`

- Raised when a value is not a valid semantic version.
+ Se lanza cuando un valor no es una versión semántica válida.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- Revolution validates input strings against the SemVer 2.0
- grammar: `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH[-prerelease][+build]`. The constructor
- records the offending `version` and a `reason: Reason`; the
- rendered message is `$version is not a valid semantic version
+ Revolution valida las cadenas de entrada con la gramática de SemVer 2.0:
+ `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH[-prerelease][+build]`. El constructor registra la `version` infractora y un
+ `reason: Reason`; el mensaje representado es `$version is not a valid semantic version

- because $reason`.
+ because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ### `↯/s.97.1.1` — `BadFormat`
+ ### `↯/s.97.1.1` — `BadFormat`

- The string did not match the SemVer grammar at all (e.g. fewer
- than three numeric components, or unrecognised separators).
+ La cadena no se ajustaba en absoluto a la gramática de SemVer (por ejemplo, menos de tres
+ componentes numéricos, o separadores no reconocidos).

- **Example.** `[↯/s.97.1.1] 1.2 is not a valid semantic version because the string did not match the SemVer 2.0 grammar`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.97.1.1] 1.2 is not a valid semantic version because the string did not match the SemVer 2.0 grammar`

- **Resolution.** Provide a fully-formed `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` string,
- optionally followed by `-prerelease` and `+build`.
+ **Solución.** Proporciona una cadena `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` completa, seguida opcionalmente de
+ `-prerelease` y `+build`.

- ### `↯/s.97.1.2` — `EmptyIdentifier`
+ ### `↯/s.97.1.2` — `EmptyIdentifier`

- The string contained a `-` or `+` separator with nothing after it
- — an empty prerelease or build identifier.
+ La cadena contenía un separador `-` o `+` sin nada detrás: un identificador de prerrelease o de
+ compilación vacío.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.97.1.2] 1.2.3- is not a valid semantic version because a prerelease or build identifier was empty`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.97.1.2] 1.2.3- is not a valid semantic version because a prerelease or build identifier was empty`

- **Resolution.** Either remove the trailing separator or supply a
- non-empty identifier after it.
+ **Solución.** Elimina el separador final o proporciona tras él un identificador no vacío.

- ### `↯/s.97.1.3` — `LeadingZero`
+ ### `↯/s.97.1.3` — `LeadingZero`

- A numeric identifier (one of `MAJOR`, `MINOR`, `PATCH`, or a
- numeric prerelease segment) had a leading zero, which SemVer
- forbids.
+ Un identificador numérico (uno de `MAJOR`, `MINOR`, `PATCH`, o un segmento numérico de
+ prerrelease) tenía un cero inicial, lo que SemVer prohíbe.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.97.1.3] 01.2.3 is not a valid semantic version because a numeric identifier had a leading zero`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.97.1.3] 01.2.3 is not a valid semantic version because a numeric identifier had a leading zero`

- **Resolution.** Strip leading zeros from numeric identifiers.
+ **Solución.** Quita los ceros iniciales de los identificadores numéricos.

- ### `↯/s.97.1.4` — `InvalidCharacter`
+ ### `↯/s.97.1.4` — `InvalidCharacter`

- A prerelease or build identifier contained a character outside
- the allowed set `[0-9A-Za-z-]`.
+ Un identificador de prerrelease o de compilación contenía un carácter fuera del conjunto
+ permitido `[0-9A-Za-z-]`.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.97.1.4] 1.2.3-alpha! is not a valid semantic version because an identifier contained a character outside [0-9A-Za-z-]`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.97.1.4] 1.2.3-alpha! is not a valid semantic version because an identifier contained a character outside [0-9A-Za-z-]`

- **Resolution.** Remove or escape the invalid character.
+ **Solución.** Elimina o escapa el carácter no válido.

